# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files - .env.example is tracked deliberately (placeholders only, no secrets)
.env*
!.env.example


# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# codegraph (local index)
/.codegraph/

# Playwright E2E
qa/e2e-report/
test-results/
# Written during a run by qa/server-intercept.mjs in count mode. A measurement
# artefact, and it is rewritten every second while a run is in progress.
qa/.intercept-tally.*.json

# Session working directory. Staging area for things passed to `--body-file`,
# `git commit -F`, and small scripts — content that ends up on GitHub or in a
# commit, not in the tree.
#
# It lives HERE rather than in a temp scratchpad on the owner's instruction,
# 2026-09-06. Temp is per-session: anything left there vanishes when the session
# ends and leaves no artefact at all — not a stale branch, not a wrong comment,
# nothing. Every other failure this project has catalogued left evidence behind.
# That one does not, which is why the files live in the repo where they can be
# seen, even though they are not tracked.
#
# STAGING, NOT STORAGE. Anything that is genuinely a document belongs in the
# repo properly and tracked.
.work/

# ── credentials and session artefacts ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# ADDED 2026-09-06 after QA found live Supabase session tokens and a script
# that mints them from .env.local sitting in a temp directory for days.
#
# They were OUTSIDE the repo, so nothing reached git - but that was luck, not
# design. `.env*` at line 34 covers the credentials themselves; nothing covered
# the ARTEFACTS a credential produces. A minted session token is as good as the
# password that made it.
#
# The owner's rule, same day: "i want everything inside codebase just put it in
# git ignored." Scratch work belongs in .work/ above - which means token files
# now land inside the repo rather than in temp, and this block is what stops
# them being committable when they do.
session*.json
session-*.json
mint-session*.mjs
*.session.json
